course: dictionary
lesson: 6459
title: Real facts and unicorn myths
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A new word often explains itself through the words around it. This is its context. «Narwhals dive to about 1,500 metres under the Arctic sea ice to hunt fish and squid.» Dive, sea ice and hunt tell you that a narwhal is an animal that lives in cold sea water and goes deep under the ice to find food.
explain: Some words are harder. «The narwhal's tusk is a tooth that grows in a spiral through its upper lip.» A tusk is a long, pointed tooth that sticks out of an animal's mouth. Spiral means it twists round and round, like a coil. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? If yes, you have probably got it.
explain: Be careful when a text seems to say something unlikely. «Long ago traders sold narwhal tusks in Europe as unicorn horns.» Unicorns are not real, so the tusk is not a horn. The sentence goes on to tell you the truth: the tusk is really a long tooth. The clues in the text can help you tell the real facts from the myths.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Narwhal» means a whale of the Arctic Ocean, with a long spiral tusk.
fact: «Tusk» means a long, pointed tooth that sticks out of the mouth.
fact: «Spiral» means winding round and round, like a coil.
fact: Narwhal tusks were sold in Europe as «unicorn horns», but the tusk is really a tooth.
exercise: «Narwhals dive to about 1,500 metres under the Arctic sea ice.» What does dive mean? | To sleep on the ice | *To go under water | To sing loudly | To fly up into the sky
exercise: «The narwhal's tusk is a tooth that grows in a spiral.» What does spiral mean? | Hidden under the sea | Straight and flat | *Winding round and round | Very cold
exercise: Which animal is a narwhal? | *A whale that lives in the Arctic Ocean | A kind of tall tree | A fish that lives in rivers | A bird that lives in deserts
test: Long ago, traders in Europe sold narwhal tusks as what? | Cups for drinking tea | Parts of ships | Lamp posts | *Unicorn horns
test: Why must narwhals find cracks in the sea ice? | *To breathe | To sing to their friends | To eat the ice | To hide from polar bears
exam: Which fact about the narwhal's tusk is true? | It is a unicorn horn that grows on a horse | *It is a tooth that can grow up to about 3 metres long | It is a fin on its back | It is a horn made of gold
